{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CuNA7Dbv7g1ji6hNj3xoE6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Phase 2 (Hardening + llm.py upgrades) â€” Description\n2\t\n3\t**North Star:** Close the two security/judgment tripwires on Aurora's LIVE verdict path AND adopt\n4\tthe cheap modern Anthropic API capabilities Aurora is missing â€” *evolving `llm.py` and the security\n5\tpath, NOT rebuilding the architecture*. This is the build half of the researchPrime AuroraTwo verdict\n6\t(`docs/AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md`): fan-out is theater at TOP_K=2-3; the value is in the LLM layer\n7\t+ the security/evidence path, both of which already exist and only need hardening/upgrading.\n8\t\n9\tTwo threads, one sequential run (they overlap on `orchestrator.py` + the security judge, so they run\n10\tin series, not parallel):\n11\t- **Security hardening (H1-H2):** payload-depth re-scan superseding the served-text backfill\n12\t  (monotonic toward non-servable); promote the evidence-rigor loop out of shadow with a real metered\n13\t  per-iteration score_fn + an engine-diff CLI + a tightened promotion gate (defaults to legacy).\n14\t- **llm.py upgrades (L1-L6):** a cost-telemetry substrate first (so discount features are metered\n15\t  correctly), then prompt caching, structured outputs, adaptive-`effort` thinking, model retargeting,\n16\t  and the Message Batches API.\n17\t\n18\t## Success criteria\n19\t- Every servable artifact carries a payload-depth `security_status`; benign-description/malicious-payload is caught; the re-stamp is monotonic toward non-servable.\n20\t- The evidence loop has a real metered per-iteration score_fn + a runnable `bin/engine-diff.py` enforcing the promotion gate; the live flip stays default-off.\n21\t- `llm.py` supports prompt caching, structured outputs, adaptive `effort`, current model tiers, and an opt-in batch path â€” all with correct CostRecorderâ†’pricing.yaml metering (regression-tested).\n22\t- Locked-prese